# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local-only notes
*.md.local

# Eval sweeps. What gets kept is the evidence a reader would check: the
# summaries carry every per-query trigger rate and every void reason, and the
# gradings carry the judge's quoted evidence per assertion. What gets dropped
# is bulk that is reproducible from the corpus and would bury the repo:
# event streams, run workspaces, and one file per individual run.
tools/eval/results/**/streams/
tools/eval/results/**/scratch/
tools/eval/results/**/workspace/
tools/eval/results/**/stream.jsonl
tools/eval/results/**/runs/
tools/eval/results/**/run.json
tools/eval/results/*.log

# Secrets and local credentials (.env.example stays tracked).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code working files (also global; repeated so clones get it too).
.claude/

# CLAUDE.md is vended here on purpose. A repo .gitignore outranks the global
# one, so this opts back in; no slash means every depth (values/CLAUDE.md).
!CLAUDE.md
